\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Filial Deity,
\par Accept my new-born cry;
\par See the travail of Thy soul,
\par Saviour, and be satisfied;
\par Take me now, possess me whole,
\par Who for me, for me, hast died.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Of life the Fountain Thou,
\par I know, I feel it now,
\par Faint and dead no more I droop:
\par Thou art in me; Thy supplies,
\par Every moment springing up,
\par Into life eternal rise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou the good Shepherd art,
\par From Thee I ne'er shall part;
\par Thou my Keeper and my Guide,
\par Make me still Thy tender care;
\par Gently lead me by Thy side,
\par Sweetly in Thy bosom bear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thou art my daily Bread;
\par O Christ, Thou art my Head;
\par Motion, virtue, strength, to me,
\par Me Thy living member, flow;
\par Nourished I, and fed by Thee,
\par Up to Thee in all things grow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Prophet, to me reveal
\par Thy Father's perfect will;
\par Never mortal spake like Thee,
\par Human prophet like divine;
\par Loud and strong their voices be,
\par Small, and still, and inward Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. On Thee, my Priest, I call,
\par Thy blood atoned for all;
\par Still the lamb as slain appears,
\par Still Thou stand'st before the throne,
\par Ever offering up my prayers,
\par These presenting with Thine own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Jesu, Thou art my King,
\par From Thee my strength I bring;
\par Shadowed by Thy mighty hand,
\par Saviour, who shall pluck me thence?
\par Faith supports; by faith I stand,
\par Strong in Thy omnipotence.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

